WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.810
After bringing you our first look at overhyped
games that ended up being terrible, we went

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.150
through your comments and suggestions. You
gave us even more potentially-great titles

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.029
that came crashing into stores on a wave of
hype and left us disappointed. Just like your

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:20.919
favorite video game franchises, we were bound
to return with a sequel.

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:22.160
Slender: The Arrival

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.089
Slender Man is one of the most celebrated
horror game characters on the Internet. The

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:30.880
villain set the standard for horrifying online
mythologies before those animal robot suits

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.660
of Five Nights at Freddy's even thought about
scaring your socks off.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.640
"Aaahhh!"

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.810
You'd think with all the Slender Man buzz,
and the occasional real-life stabbing in his

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:45.480
name, any game starring the message board
monster would have to be worthwhile. Instead,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.590
Slender: The Arrival tries to skate by on
a creepy atmosphere and an occasionally-spooky

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:55.660
bad guy. The gameplay is simplified to collecting
note pages and turning on generators while

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.220
avoiding the creeps stalking you. The game’s
main villain occasionally teleports around

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:05.100
and can be seen staring at you in the distance...
until he appears nearby and jump-scares you.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.920
That's about it. At least the game helped
inspire releases like Alien: Isolation. But

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.329
Slender: The Arrival was way too overhyped
to justify its underwhelming premise.

00:01:14.329 --> 00:01:15.350
Fable III

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.899
Following in the footsteps of its predecessors,
Fable 3's expansive world was filled with

00:01:19.899 --> 00:01:24.289
charm. But that doesn't necessarily save it
from its obvious shortcomings. Most of the

00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:27.999
game’s familiar RPG aspects were tossed
out the window for the sake of making things

00:01:27.999 --> 00:01:33.319
easier for the casual gamer. Worse, the gameplay
was plagued with more bugs than the streetwalkers

00:01:33.319 --> 00:01:34.770
in Bowerstone.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.219
Even with an all-star voice cast featuring
Simon Pegg and Michael Fassbender, Fable 3's

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:43.999
technical problems and simplified gameplay
hamper any potential enjoyment. Even the game’s

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:49.619
final scenario makes you defend the entire
country from invasion… using money. And

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:53.399
it’s no easy sum to attain if you’ve played
the game properly. This ends things with an

00:01:53.399 --> 00:01:58.219
unsatisfying letdown for those who cleared
the Fable trilogy, with no future installments

00:01:58.219 --> 00:01:59.359
in sight.

00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:00.879
(roar)

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.939
The Order: 1886

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:08.630
In spite of its cinematic look, creative weapons,
and unique story, The Order: 1886's generic

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:13.439
gameplay didn’t end up being Sony's answer
to Gears of War, despite early expectations.

00:02:13.439 --> 00:02:18.290
It’s another case of visuals getting prioritized
over gameplay. It doesn't help that the story

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:23.670
is linear and offers no replay value, making
it feel like a rental at best... Or worse,

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.790
an extended PlayStation demo. There are too
many quick time events to make you ever feel

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:32.689
like you're in control of anything meaningful.
Despite werewolves, zeppelins, Tesla-powered

00:02:32.689 --> 00:02:37.829
weapons, and great graphics, there's not much
else here. Once promised to be a huge system-seller

00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:42.970
for the PlayStation 4, The Order just ended
up being short for Order Another Game Because

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.210
This One Sucks.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:44.940
(gunshot)

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.040
Sonic Boom: Rise of Lyric

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.569
After the fiasco of 2006’s Sonic the Hedgehog,
we thought Sega would never be able to bring

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:59.260
Sonic back to proper form. For 2014's Rise
of Lyric, Sega completely redesigned the Sonic

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:05.459
crew, giving them lankier limbs, useless athletic
tape, random fashion accessories… And possibly

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:10.299
steroids. Ultimately, Rise of Lyric boils
down to what we were dreading the most: Another

00:03:10.299 --> 00:03:12.769
lousy 3D Sonic game.

00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:17.650
Even with a successful TV series to help build
up the revamped Sonic squad, Rise of Lyric

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:22.590
falls on its face. Many of the game's segments
are hampered by an extremely basic combat

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:26.680
system. There’s also a weird laser called
“Enerbeam” that’s shoehorned into the

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.810
game way too many times. In an era where Mario
has successfully made the jump to 3D multiple

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.930
times, we're afraid this is going to be the
final nail in the Sonic-coffin. Sega should

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.079
just sell the rights to Nintendo already.

00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:39.920
Tony Hawk Pro Skater 5

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.159
We had high hopes that returning to the Pro
Skater series would mean we’d finally get

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:48.900
a good skateboarding game again. But we were
wrong. After developer Neversoft left the

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:54.620
Tony Hawk franchise, Robomodo took over in
2010, producing games so bad that the whole

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.999
franchise was put on hold. Somehow, Robomodo
reclaimed the reins for Pro Skater 5, along

00:03:59.999 --> 00:04:05.159
with co-developer Disruptive Games...but adding
another studio didn't make the game any better.

00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:10.730
Pro Skater 5 is filled with embarrassing glitches,
outdated visuals, terrible controls, erratic

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:15.400
obstacle clipping, and uninspired gameplay.
The game’s marketing was entirely based

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.209
on the franchise name and the professional
boarders featured on the roster, but you'll

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:23.870
have more fun just watching other gamers show
off its endless bugs on YouTube. Pro Skater

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:28.389
5 is easily the worst game of the series and
a blatant attempt to cash in on the memories

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:30.560
of a once-beloved series.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.810
Star Wars Battlefront

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:36.030
Even though it had all the ingredients of
a great game, Star Wars Battlefront ultimately

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.780
failed to deliver. Given developer DICE’s
history with the successful Battlefield series,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:45.139
fans expected multiplayer goodness on the
same level as Battlefield 4. Throw in the

00:04:45.139 --> 00:04:49.770
Star Wars Battlefront franchise, and we were
bound for something both nerdy and groundbreaking,

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:55.030
right? Battlefront ended up being all sizzle
and no steak. It’s easily one of the greatest-looking

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:59.639
first-person shooters ever made, but it's
also one of the shallowest.

00:04:59.639 --> 00:05:03.250
Thousands of players voiced their unhappiness
with the game, resulting in lukewarm scores

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:07.970
on Metacritic and elsewhere. Excluding the
tutorials, almost all of Battlefront focuses

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:12.610
on online multiplayer. Despite a collection
of familiar multiplayer modes, everything

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:17.800
just boils down to the same kind of mid-range
firefight, which can get old fast. After playing

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.030
Battlefront for 30 minutes, you've pretty
much experienced all the game has to offer.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:25.460
This game has a shorter life than one of Jabba’s
dancers.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.430
Assassin's Creed Unity

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:31.660
Despite being a perfect opportunity for Ubisoft
to push modern consoles to their limits, Assassin’s

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.470
Creed Unity ended up offering more of the
same kind of stuff that we saw out of the

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:41.080
franchise back in 2007. It doesn't have the
awesome pirate motif of Black Flag, and the

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:45.599
French Revolution backdrop gets pretty stagnant.
While it's cool to see thousands of revolting

00:05:45.599 --> 00:05:49.949
citizens on the streets, it's underwhelming
to watch the same thing happening down every

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:50.919
city block.

00:05:50.919 --> 00:05:55.690
If that weren't bad enough, Unity is made
much, much worse because of its numerous technical

00:05:55.690 --> 00:06:02.800
issues. Seriously, it has a ton of glitches.
No, seriously...so many glitches. Some of

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.590
these bugs are simple visual stutters, but
there’s much worse. A glitch where the faces

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:11.500
of the characters don't show up, but their
hair, eyes, and teeth do? It's as frightening

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:16.629
as you'd imagine. Still, nothing beats having
the game glitch just before your big assassination

00:06:16.629 --> 00:06:21.340
attempt on a high profile target. Did Ubisoft
delay the sequel because of these issues?

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:25.389
Of course not. Assassin's Creed Syndicate
launched less than a year later.

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:26.580
Watch Dogs

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:31.419
Watch Dogs was one of the most highly anticipated
launch games for the PS4 and Xbox One, but

00:06:31.419 --> 00:06:35.669
it simply failed to deliver. Sure, gamers
could hack their way through an open-world

00:06:35.669 --> 00:06:40.150
version of Chicago. But after playing for
a few hours, nobody really wanted to.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:45.370
A lot of the fundamental elements of Watch
Dogs simply aren't that good. Crappy controls.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:49.220
Vehicles that handle like a tractor trailer
hovercraft, no matter what you're driving.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.919
And that's a major problem, given how much
driving you have to do. Also filled with tons

00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:58.759
of repetitive side missions. So let's see,
poor controls, horrible driving, and crappy

00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:04.020
stealth sequences, Watch Dogs probably should've
been sent to obedience school.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.180
Enter the Matrix

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:10.110
Remember how amazing that first Matrix movie
was? Well, the video game that came afterwards,

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:14.810
Enter the Matrix, is where hope goes to die.
The title was a tie-in with the release of

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:19.289
the first movie sequel, The Matrix Reloaded,
which received similarly mixed reactions from

00:07:19.289 --> 00:07:24.060
fans and critics. As a result, Enter the Matrix
was rushed to launch the same week that the

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:28.710
film hit theaters, and it shows. Any game
set in the world of The Matrix comes with

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:33.639
some pretty simple expectations. Among them:
being able to play as the movie's heroes,

00:07:33.639 --> 00:07:38.419
like Neo, Morpheus, or Trinity, while fighting
with stylized moves and slowed-down action

00:07:38.419 --> 00:07:43.220
sequences. You know, all the stuff that made
people like the movie in the first place.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:48.610
Instead, you end up playing as Niobe or Ghost:
two insignificant characters from Reloaded.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:52.379
The third-person fighting had a lot of promise,
especially when you factor in your bullet

00:07:52.379 --> 00:07:56.639
time abilities, but it gets old quickly. Sure,
it was kind of interesting that Enter the

00:07:56.639 --> 00:08:00.919
Matrix helped tell the side stories of what
happened around the events of Reloaded. Too

00:08:00.919 --> 00:08:04.379
bad Reloaded wasn't much better than a crummy
video game on its own.

00:08:04.379 --> 00:08:08.220
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.530
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which hyped-up games you think were

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:13.519
the absolute worst...

